  "sourceFindings": [
    "Prayer 425–445 adds twenty-one complete numbered reports, sixty English segments and seventeen complete source chapters (55–71). All twenty-four selected Arabic paragraphs remain unchanged. Chapter 55 is untitled in the selected source and both inspected Arabic prints; the app does not invent a thematic heading.",
    "Historical print PDF pages 120–126 and modern print PDF pages 118–123 were visually inspected. Modern labels 435–457 include a combined 435–436 label for selected 425 and separate 454 and 455 numbers within selected 443. Every selected report was compared individually. English EPUB labels 1.8.427–1.8.447 are individually hash-bound to the pinned records; this local mapping is not a universal offset.",
    "Bewley 427 is explicitly marked as an abbreviated comparison: it only refers to 328. The earlier target in the Book of Tayammum was read separately and linked as comparison evidence. Its different order and additional wording do not replace selected 427. Intercession remains last in selected 427.",
    "428 preserves all four paragraphs: the complete accusation account, narrator alternatives, two verse lines and the closing Aisha exchange. The selected أعاجيب remains despite تعاجيب in both prints. The shifts between first- and third-person narration remain, and jewels from the English comparisons are not inserted. Wishah stays a provisional transliteration. The no-family wording at 429 has a separate note recording Ibn Hajar’s narrower wife and broader relatives readings.",
    "432 and 439 keep narrator uncertainty as visible transmission notes in source order. 433 retains al-Sulami despite al-Aslami in the English EPUB. 435 retains all three construction stages and distinct building materials. Lexical choices and printed differences are recorded separately from the source text.",
    "436 retains The rebellious group will kill him, present in the selected Arabic, both inspected Arabic prints and Bewley but omitted from the checked EPUB quotation. No added faction identity is imported. 440 retains Sufyan’s question to Amr without inserting the Yes found in a later parallel. 441 retains both Abu Burdah links, and 442 does not insert a personal-name explanation for Holy Spirit.",
    "443 preserves both complete chains and reports as one selected entry; the spears detail appears only in its second account. 444 retains both Sufyan variants and all three closing transmission attributions in selected order, including the shortened Malik statement. Its wording follows لمن أعتق, the one who sets free, rather than the checked EPUB’s manumitted wording. It preserves a hundred times without inserting a hundred conditions.",
